<section id="pf-assess" class="pf-section pf-reveal">
  <p class="pf-step-tag">Step 2 · Inside view</p>
  <h2><span class="pf-section-number">04</span> Assess political feasibility</h2>
  <p class="pf-prose">
    The inside view assesses each trajectory across the five dimensions. This can be done by a single researcher or by a team of modellers. The
    ratings below are my judgements, based on the sources listed under each dimension and available up to October 2026. They are a starting point and
    can be revised as new evidence appears.
  </p>
  <p class="pf-caption pf-rating-legend">
    <span>{% include policy-feasibility/rating.liquid rating='favourable' %} favourable</span>
    <span>{% include policy-feasibility/rating.liquid rating='mixed' %} mixed</span>
    <span>{% include policy-feasibility/rating.liquid rating='unfavourable' %} unfavourable</span>
  </p>
  <div class="pf-table-scroll">
    <table class="pf-profile">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Dimension</th>
          {% for t in pf.trajectories %}
            <th scope="col" data-trajectory="{{ t.id }}">
              <span class="pf-swatch" aria-hidden="true"></span><small>{{ t.id }}</small>{{ t.short_title }}
            </th>
          {% endfor %}
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {% for d in pf.dimensions %}
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">
              <a href="#pf-dimension-{{ d.id }}">{{ d.name }}</a>
            </th>
            {% for t in pf.trajectories %}
              {% assign cell = t.profile[d.id] %}
              <td data-trajectory="{{ t.id }}" data-label="{{ t.id }} {{ t.short_title }}">
                {% include policy-feasibility/rating.liquid rating=cell.rating %}
                <span class="pf-profile-text">{{ cell.text }}</span>
              </td>
            {% endfor %}
          </tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h3 class="pf-evidence-heading">Evidence, dimension by dimension</h3>
  <div class="pf-drawers">
    {% for d in pf.dimensions %}
      <details class="pf-drawer pf-dimension" id="pf-dimension-{{ d.id }}">
        <summary>
          <strong>{{ d.name }}</strong><span>{{ d.guide }}</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="pf-dimension-body">
          <p class="pf-caption">{{ d.description }}</p>
          <div class="pf-evidence-columns">
            {% for t in pf.trajectories %}
              {% assign c = d.cells[t.id] %}
              <article data-trajectory="{{ t.id }}">
                <h4>
                  <span class="pf-swatch" aria-hidden="true"></span><small>{{ t.id }}</small>{{ t.short_title }}
                </h4>
                <p>{{ c.assessment }}</p>
                {% if c.uncertainty %}
                  <p class="pf-take-forward">{{ c.uncertainty }}</p>
                {% endif %}
                {% include policy-feasibility/references.liquid ids=c.evidence %}
              </article>
            {% endfor %}
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>

  <p class="pf-prose pf-pairwise-note">
    In a workshop, the assessment can also be done in pairs. The team compares two trajectories one dimension at a time and notes which of the two has
    the better chance of being adopted, and why. The article describes this in Section 4.5, based on
    <a href="{{ pf.pairwise_reference.url }}">Carlson and Montgomery (2017)</a>. I have not done it on this page.
  </p>
  {% include policy-feasibility/next.liquid href='#pf-model' number='05' title='Bring the assessment into the scenario' %}
</section>
